H3-Chat includes open-source components with their own licenses.

Document import includes pinned pypdf, python-docx, lxml, pypdfium2/PDFium,
Pillow, NumPy and typing-extensions wheels. Infographic rendering uses the
private PyAV (BSD-3-Clause), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause) and Pillow (MIT-CMU) packages;
their original notices remain in the installed wheel folders. Microsoft Edge
is provided by Windows and is not redistributed by H3-Chat.
Speech transcription optionally installs
Faster Whisper, CTranslate2, PyAV, ONNX Runtime and their pinned dependencies.
Upstream provenance is in scripts/tools-sources.json; original licenses/notices
remain in runtime/tools package folders. Private Microsoft CRT files retain
the license and provenance in native/redist/NOTICE.txt and SOURCES.json.
Whisper model weights are MIT-licensed upstream and are not bundled.

llama.cpp and stable-diffusion.cpp: MIT; copyright their respective contributors.
Python: Python Software Foundation License, included in runtime/python/LICENSE.txt.
Manrope and Cormorant: SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Frontend dependencies and their notices are in licenses/ and package-lock.json.
Bundled JavaScript preserves esbuild's legal notices in static/app.js.LEGAL.txt.

Model weights are not part of the release archive. Their licenses are shown in
catalog.json and link to their original model repositories. Application licensing
does not replace or relax model license terms.

H3-Chat is an independent application. The names of upstream projects identify
compatibility and do not imply endorsement.

The H3 image worker vendors the stable-diffusion.cpp C API header at commit 7f410a3,
nlohmann/json (MIT), stb_image and stb_image_write (MIT/public-domain dual license).
Source URLs and SHA-256 hashes are recorded in native/vendor/SOURCES.json.
Each vendored header retains its upstream copyright and license notice.

The optional Ming / Qwen 2.1 image worker (native/vision-worker.py), MiniMax H3
video worker (native/video-worker.py) and their ComfyUI
inference library are GPL-3.0-or-later. The optional runtime includes complete
unmodified core source, licenses and Python distribution notices. See
docs/vision-engine.md and runtime/vision/SOURCES.json. No model weights are bundled.

The optional vision runtime includes Microsoft Visual C++ Redistributable CRT
libraries. These unmodified system libraries retain their Microsoft license.
See runtime/vision/dlls/NOTICE.txt. They are not covered by the application MIT
license or the image worker GPL license.

The private YuE2 music workers use audio.cpp (Apache-2.0) at commit
13c4192a28d6a212f075c4cbefc5e4983e6ed52a, with the H3 artifact patch.
See docs/music-engine.md, native/music/h3-artifacts.patch and each runtime's
SOURCES.json and retained upstream license files. GGML is MIT licensed;
SentencePiece and its dependencies retain their individual notices.
Microsoft Visual C++ redistributables and NVIDIA CUDA redistributables retain
their separate vendor licenses; neither is relicensed under MIT.
YuE2 model weights are not bundled and are licensed CC BY-NC 4.0.

The CPU/CUDA/Vulkan native engines also use app-local Microsoft Visual C++ CRT
libraries. See native/redist/NOTICE.txt and SOURCES.json for version, origin and
checksums. These Microsoft libraries are not relicensed under MIT.

Optional Manim rendering uses the pinned Python wheels listed in
scripts/lab-sources.json and runtimes.json (tools_lab). Individual upstream
licenses are retained in licenses/lab-* and in the installed distributions.
The unmodified srt 3.5.3 module is vendored under MIT (licenses/srt.txt).
No system TeX, Python, or FFmpeg installation is required for supported scenes;
formula rendering uses Matplotlib MathText and video encoding uses PyAV.
EmbeddingGemma weights are optional and governed by the Gemma terms; no weights
are included in the app or release package.

The optional video accelerator uses upstream SageAttention Windows wheels
(Apache-2.0), Triton Windows (MIT) and CPython include/import libraries (PSF).
Pinned URLs and checksums are in runtimes.json; licenses remain in the installed
wheel distributions. See docs/video-engine.md. These are app-local components
and do not use another application's Python or ComfyUI installation.

Full Manim Python rendering optionally uses TinyTeX/TeX Live 2026.10
(https://github.com/rstudio/tinytex-releases, upstream licenses retained) and
dvisvgm 3.6 (GPL-3.0-or-later; licenses/dvisvgm-GPL-3.txt). Binary provenance and
source links: scripts/latex-sources.json. These optional downloads are not
bundled in the portable application ZIP. Legacy storyboard formulas continue
to use Matplotlib MathText; full Python Tex/MathTex uses the real TeX compiler.

Voice: speech adapter and controls adapted from H3-Audio (MIT, licenses/H3-Audio-MIT.txt).
Higgs Audio v2 codec adapted from Transformers 5.14.1 (Apache-2.0); copyright Boson AI and HuggingFace.
Pure PyTorch resampling from TorchAudio 2.7.1 (BSD-2-Clause, licenses/TorchAudio-LICENSE.txt).
Model weights and voice reference recordings are not redistributed.


Qwen Image 2.1 Turbo is an optional separately downloaded model under the Qwen Research License. The INT8 ConvRot transformer and compatible encoder/VAE are distributed by Comfy-Org/Qwen-Image-2.1; original model: Qwen/Qwen-Image-2.1-Turbo. Model weights are not included in the application package.
